# SAHACHARA OS — COMPLETE SYSTEM WORKFLOW, PRODUCT ARCHITECTURE AND UI REDESIGN MASTER PROMPT

## 1. YOUR ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a principal product designer, senior UX architect, healthcare SaaS specialist, and senior frontend engineer.

Build a completely new UI/UX for Sahachara OS, an Ayurvedic healthcare operations management platform. The goal is to experiment with a new visual design and information architecture while preserving the existing system's business logic, workflows, data relationships, authentication rules, authorization model, and operational capabilities.

This is a UI redesign and implementation project, not a request to invent a new healthcare system.

The application should feel like a premium, modern, enterprise-grade healthcare operating system rather than a conventional clinic management dashboard.

The final result must be a cohesive, functional application with connected pages, realistic workflows, reusable components, proper navigation, responsive layouts, and consistent interaction patterns.

Do not build only a landing page or a collection of disconnected mockup screens. Build the application shell and all required internal screens.

## 2. CRITICAL PROJECT RULES

Before making any changes:

1. Inspect the existing project files, package configuration, framework, routing structure, components, styling, database integration, authentication, API endpoints, and existing workflows.
2. Identify the existing application's actual capabilities and distinguish implemented features from proposed features.
3. Reuse the existing technology stack, dependencies, authentication system, data models, APIs, and business logic wherever available.
4. Do not replace the backend or database.
5. Do not introduce a new authentication provider or modify authentication behavior.
6. Do not modify database schemas, migrations, API contracts, environment variables, authorization rules, or business logic simply to make the new UI easier to build.
7. Do not remove existing functionality.
8. Do not replace working backend integrations with hardcoded arrays, fake APIs, or local-only data.
9. If a backend feature is unavailable, build the appropriate frontend interface and clearly separate the presentation layer from the future integration point.
10. Never display fake success messages for operations that have not actually succeeded.
11. Do not invent existing routes, database columns, API endpoints, or permissions. Discover them from the project.
12. Do not introduce patient data into public URLs, browser storage, logs, or unnecessary client-side caches.
13. Preserve all existing security protections, server-side authorization, and organization boundaries.
14. Complete the UI implementation rather than stopping after an audit or design proposal.

The existing system is the source of truth for implemented behavior. This specification defines the intended product experience and functional coverage.

If the current system has different naming or workflows, preserve the actual implemented behavior and adapt the UI accordingly.

## 3. PRODUCT OVERVIEW

Sahachara OS is an Ayurvedic healthcare operations platform that connects patient registration, appointments, consultations, Ayurvedic assessments, treatment plans, Panchakarma courses, therapy sessions, prescriptions, pharmacy inventory, dispensing, invoicing, payments, receipts, reporting, staff management, and system administration.

The core patient journey is:

Patient Registration → Appointment Booking → Patient Check-In → Consultation → Clinical Assessment → Ayurvedic Assessment → Treatment Plan → Therapy or Panchakarma → Prescription → Pharmacy Dispensing → Invoice → Payment → Receipt → Follow-Up → Reporting.

Not every patient must complete every stage. The system must support existing workflow variations, standalone appointments, follow-ups, treatments, prescriptions, billing, and other operations as permitted by the existing backend.

Every module should connect to the relevant patient, appointment, consultation, treatment, prescription, invoice, or payment record.

